WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.868
-You guys, our first guest
tonight is

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:05.105
a Grammy Award-winning
multiplatinum musician.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:09.142
Her makeup line GXVE Beauty
is available now.

00:00:09.142 --> 00:00:13.279
[ Laughter ]

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.281
At Sephora and gxvebeauty.com.

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:18.584
She also returns as a coach on
the new season of "The Voice,"

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:21.053
which premieres September 19th
at 8:00 p.m. on NBC.

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.623
Let's take a look.
-I have toured the world.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.126
I know how to do this show.
And it's kind of a two for one

00:00:27.126 --> 00:00:29.062
'cause I'll just ask him
if I have questions.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:29.962
[ Laughter ]
So it's fine either way.

00:00:29.962 --> 00:00:32.098
-You wish. You wish.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.866
-Anyways, I thought you did
a great job.

00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:35.301
And I would love to coach you

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.003
if you want to be over here on
Team Gwen.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.337
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.306
our friend Gwen Stefani,
everybody.

00:00:40.306 --> 00:00:41.941
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:49.081 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:56.188 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:56.188 --> 00:00:57.757
Welcome back!

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:59.692
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:01.394
-This is so --

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.364
I feel like the last couple
of years just evaporated.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:06.065
It's been like two years.
-I know.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:07.900
Well, we've seen each other
on Zoom.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.902
You've been kind enough
to do the show that way.

00:01:09.902 --> 00:01:11.704
But it's been three years since
you've been here in person.

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.405
-Three years, oh, my gosh.
-It's so nice to have you back.

00:01:13.405 --> 00:01:15.407
-That's so crazy.
-How has your summer been?

00:01:15.407 --> 00:01:17.543
I know you were on the road
with Blake. How's that?

00:01:17.543 --> 00:01:18.911
-It's been really fun.

00:01:18.911 --> 00:01:22.081
And it's something I never
thought would ever happen to me.

00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:25.919
We actually -- He invited me
to be on a couple of his tracks.

00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:27.887
A couple duets or whatever.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.856
And they went to number one
country radio, so --

00:01:29.856 --> 00:01:33.092
-Yeah. I guess you wouldn't have
predicted even 10 years ago --

00:01:33.092 --> 00:01:36.429
-I wouldn't predicted
ever meeting Blake Shelton,

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:40.433
let alone being on the road with
him and hopping on his stage.

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:43.335
It's been really fun.
-And so, obviously, Blake --

00:01:43.335 --> 00:01:47.006
I feel like Blake and No Doubt
maybe have different fan bases.

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.875
But are there times --
Does he --

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:51.310
-You'd be surprised.
-Yeah.

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:53.012
-We're definitely
cross-pollinating.

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.979
-That's good.
-Yeah.

00:01:53.979 --> 00:01:56.182
-Do you ever do
any of your songs

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.750
when you're on the road
with Blake?
-You know what?

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.486
He asks me
to do songs all the time.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.455
And I'm like,
"It's not my stage."

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.823
Like, "This is so awkward."

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.525
Like I'm forcing myself like,
"I want some attention.

00:02:06.525 --> 00:02:08.127
Let me be on your --"
It's not.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:09.829
But he wants me to come on.

00:02:09.829 --> 00:02:12.031
And sometimes I'll do, like,
"Don't Speak."

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.833
-Yeah.
-And it's pretty incredible

00:02:13.833 --> 00:02:17.136
to be able to have a song that
you get out there and you think,

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:19.839
"Do they know me? Are they going
to be like, 'Why is she here?'"

00:02:19.839 --> 00:02:21.174
Then they know all the words.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.841
You're like, "Oh, my God.
This is crazy."

00:02:22.841 --> 00:02:24.510
-That's great.
I mean, I guess with songs

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.746
that iconic, they do cross over,
you know,

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:29.215
all genre of fan I guess.
-That song is just --

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.484
it's that song
that just went everywhere.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:33.353
-And I would imagine
you might be thinking,

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:35.821
"I'm not here
to steal your focus."

00:02:35.821 --> 00:02:38.090
But I would imagine an audience
loses their mind

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.092
when they think, "I'm lucky
enough I'm getting two for one."

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.361
-Well, I feel like --
We were up in, like, Canada,

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.296
somewhere I never even heard of.
And I'm like --

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:47.166
I wasn't even going to go up.
I'm like, "Not today."

00:02:47.166 --> 00:02:49.635
I was like, "How do I not?"
You know?

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.671
I'm never going to be there
again, so I do it.

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.806
-Do you get worried when you've
never heard of a place

00:02:53.806 --> 00:02:55.408
that you're going to be like,
"Are you ready to rock?"

00:02:55.408 --> 00:02:56.909
and then forget
the name of the place?

00:02:56.909 --> 00:02:57.943
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.943 --> 00:02:59.946
-All the time.

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:01.747
I'm scared I'm going to forget

00:03:01.747 --> 00:03:02.982
your name right now
at this point.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:06.152
[ Laughter ]
-Just say, "Hey, buddy."

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:08.754
I respond to that really well.
-Okay.

00:03:08.754 --> 00:03:11.591
-So, you have not done a couple
seasons of "The Voice."

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:13.693
But the last one you did,
you won.

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:15.394
-Winner! Yep.
-Yeah, congratulations.

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.664
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:18.664 --> 00:03:21.400
Do you feel more relaxed
having a win like that,

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.735
a recent win under your belt?

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:24.804
-Winning is fun.

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.172
I think the thing --
The way I won was amazing

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:29.642
because I actually had
a 14-year-old boy.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.544
And he was a one-chair turn.

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:33.846
So, these ears heard a star.

00:03:33.846 --> 00:03:34.947
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:03:34.947 --> 00:03:36.682
-That's really nice.
-It was cool.

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:38.183
And he turned 15 on the show.

00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:41.086
And, you know, when you see him
now, his name is Carter Rubin.

00:03:41.086 --> 00:03:42.788
Check him out. He's incredible.

00:03:42.788 --> 00:03:45.791
He's just grown before my eyes
like he's my kid.

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.527
And he's blossomed, and --

00:03:47.527 --> 00:03:49.228
So yeah, I mean,
we don't really win.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.130
It's them who win. But it was
really fun to coach him.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:52.598
-I don't know.
You definitely said "winner"

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:54.200
real quick and did this thing.
-That is true.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.701
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.837
-I really feel like you're
changing the narrative.

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.338
And we were all here
when you did that.

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:00.806
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.806 --> 00:04:03.642
-It does feel good to have one
under my belt when I go back.

00:04:03.642 --> 00:04:06.045
There's no way to compete with
Blake Shelton.

00:04:06.045 --> 00:04:08.680
-Yes. But it must be nice, yeah.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.083
-It's fun to rub it in
when I come back, yeah.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:14.020
-He seems very -- He seems to be
someone who both enjoys

00:04:14.020 --> 00:04:16.889
the rubbing
and the being rubbed against.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:20.526
-I love rubbing him.
It's so fun. He's rubbable.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:24.730
-So, you obviously,
before No Doubt's time,

00:04:24.730 --> 00:04:26.298
you had been doing music
forever.

00:04:26.298 --> 00:04:28.968
So you were never in a situation
where you had to audition

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.503
for anyone the way
"The Voice" singers do.

00:04:31.503 --> 00:04:33.873
-That's true.
I always think about that.

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:37.343
I did audition to be
a cheerleader in high school,

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.744
and I didn't make it.
-You didn't? Really?

00:04:38.744 --> 00:04:39.979
-Didn't even make the first --

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.480
I can't believe
they even let me try out.

00:04:41.480 --> 00:04:43.783
I tried out. I really just
wanted to wear the outfit.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:45.284
-Sure.
-That was the whole thing.

00:04:45.284 --> 00:04:46.519
So, I kind of made up for it.

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:49.321
-Did you know
while you were auditioning,

00:04:49.321 --> 00:04:50.889
"This isn't going well"?

00:04:50.889 --> 00:04:54.860
-I knew that I wasn't able to do
choreography like that.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.929
I couldn't remember. Remember,
we just talked about that?

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.165
-Yeah.
-So, I had a hard time

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.834
remembering the moves, and --
but yeah --

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:04.837
-It did work out. You found
a different way into the outfit.

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:08.040
-I got the outfit.
-In the "Hollaback" video.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.944
Do you think that
the cheerleading coach saw this

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.614
and was like,
"You went around --

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:16.816
you didn't go through
proper channels!"

00:05:16.816 --> 00:05:19.351
-I don't even know.
I do think about that.

00:05:19.351 --> 00:05:22.221
I wonder who that person was,
and if they were like,

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:24.090
"Wow, she cheated her way
to the top."

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.992
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.992 --> 00:05:28.994
-But now you're also --
Marching band costume as well.

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:31.897
-Yes.
-Were you in marching band?

00:05:31.897 --> 00:05:33.733
-I was. I was a band geek.

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:36.335
And I fake-played the piccolo
for a long time.

00:05:36.335 --> 00:05:39.304
-Okay, so, what do you mean
by fake played?

00:05:39.304 --> 00:05:41.240
-Well, I'm not a liar.

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:43.275
But I definitely
couldn't really --

00:05:43.275 --> 00:05:44.710
-A lot of the time you spend
telling us what you're not.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.111
-I cheated.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:46.111 --> 00:05:48.848
-You've also told us
what you are.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:50.749
-Okay, well, I did --
-You cheated?

00:05:50.749 --> 00:05:54.687
-I just never could get the hang
of playing that instrument.

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:57.556
-And they just never noticed
you were fake playing?

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:01.060
-There's a lot of people
in the band, right?

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.862
And I was a piccolo!
-Do you feel like this is

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:04.930
a problem across marching bands
across America,

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:06.766
that there are just
a lot of piccolo players

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.467
who are just faking it?
-I hope not.

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:09.902
-I hope not.
-I hope not.

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:12.004
I had a lot of fun doing that,
though. That was incredible.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:15.374
I wanted to be the dancer,
but I was in a band uniform.

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:17.042
-Gotcha. Well, that's a good way
to start.

00:06:17.042 --> 00:06:19.912
'Cause there is some -- I mean,
I'm not being insincere.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:21.947
There is a lot of choreography
for marching bands as well.

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:23.816
-It's a lot of choreography.
-Yeah.

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.851
-Yeah, and I cannot dance.

00:06:25.851 --> 00:06:29.621
People think that I can dance,
but I just fake that as well.

00:06:29.621 --> 00:06:32.091
-Well, you're very good
at all of this.

00:06:32.091 --> 00:06:34.026
-I'm very sneaky, yeah.

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.862
-Are you really married
to Blake Shelton?

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:37.029
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.531
Because it looks that way on TV.

00:06:38.531 --> 00:06:40.733
-This is a fake diamond ring.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:44.404
-I got more to ask you. We'll be
right back with Gwen Stefani.

